  32:common/prog/dbus/dbusdll.h **** 
  33:common/prog/dbus/dbusdll.h **** \section introDLL Data Link Layer for D-Bus-2
  34:common/prog/dbus/dbusdll.h **** 
  35:common/prog/dbus/dbusdll.h ****      This layer handles the message reception and transmission close to the bus-hardware, handling 
  36:common/prog/dbus/dbusdll.h ****         - wrapping the message data into a frame as described below, which includes message legth,
  37:common/prog/dbus/dbusdll.h ****         TargetAddress, MessageIdentifier, the data of the message and the attached CRC (16 bit),
  38:common/prog/dbus/dbusdll.h ****         all followed by an acknowledgement from the receiving node (or sending node by broadcasts).
  39:common/prog/dbus/dbusdll.h **** 
  40:common/prog/dbus/dbusdll.h ****      An incoming message will be acknowledged by the data link layer if the current node (communica
  41:common/prog/dbus/dbusdll.h ****      On default only one communication partner address is used, but it is possible to replace the d
  42:common/prog/dbus/dbusdll.h ****      allow more addresses to be accepted by the current node.
  43:common/prog/dbus/dbusdll.h **** 
  44:common/prog/dbus/dbusdll.h **** E.g. Communication partner 1 may also respond to messages sent to communication partner Ah (decimal
  45:common/prog/dbus/dbusdll.h **** However, the acknowledgement generated by the node will always use the same address for identificat
  46:common/prog/dbus/dbusdll.h **** communication partner 1 (i.e. if communication partner Ah is addressed, communication partner 1 wil
  47:common/prog/dbus/dbusdll.h **** 
  48:common/prog/dbus/dbusdll.h **** Frame: \image html dbusdll.gif
  49:common/prog/dbus/dbusdll.h **** 
  50:common/prog/dbus/dbusdll.h **** */
